 ## Overview
-Volume Utility Functions are a collection of low-level helper routines used to prepare, validate, and transform volumetric data for compression and rendering pipelines. They solve problems related to tensor dimensionality alignment, physical unit normalization (Hounsfield units), spatial resampling, and memory layout corrections. Unlike [Sparse structures](5-sparse-structures.md) which organize data topology, or [Value compression](6-value-compression.md) which reduces bit-depth, these utilities ensure data integrity and format compatibility before compression or rendering occurs. They serve as the foundational preprocessing and postprocessing steps for the [Compression](4-compression.md) pipeline.
+Volume Utility Functions prepare volumetric data for the [Compression](4-compression.md) pipeline by addressing distinct aspects of data integrity and range mapping [Parent]. They handle tensor dimensionality alignment via `make_nd` [S1, unofficial], physical unit normalization via `normalize_hounsfield` [S1, unofficial], spatial resampling via `normalize_voxel_scale` [S1, unofficial], and memory/layout corrections [S3, S4, unofficial][S6][S7, S8, unofficial]. Unlike [Sparse structures](5-sparse-structures.md) which organize data topology, or [Value compression](6-value-compression.md) which reduces bit-depth, these utilities ensure data integrity and format compatibility before compression or rendering occurs.
 
