 ### make_nd
-Prepends singleton dimensions to a tensor until it reaches a target dimensionality $n$.
-
-**Inputs:**
-- `t`: Input tensor of dimensionality $t.ndim$.
-- `n`: Target dimensionality (integer).
-
-**Outputs:**
-- Tensor of dimensionality $n$.
-
+**Inputs:** `t` (tensor/array), `n` (integer target dimensionality).
+**Outputs:** Tensor of dimensionality `n`.
 **Steps:**
-1. If $n < t.ndim$, raise an exception.
-2. While $t.ndim < n$:
-   - Prepend a dimension of size 1 to `t`.
+1. If $n < \text{len}(t.\text{shape})$, raise an exception.
+2. While $\text{len}(t.\text{shape}) < n$, prepend a dimension of size 1 to `t`.
 3. Return `t`.
